{"v": 1, "ts": "2026-08-14T01:16:00Z", "actor": "orchestrator", "type": "process_finding", "ref_id": "CHANGE-0144", "finding": "I wrote the intake with frontmatter id spec-vagueness-gate, identical to the spec's id, breaking the repo convention that an intake carries the bare slug and the spec carries the spec- prefix (see CHANGE-0142: followup-registry vs spec-followup-registry). Consequence: docs-audit reported a duplicate doc id and every id-keyed tool degraded - the TDD role could not run docs-audit --gate <id> at all (exit 2, ambiguous id) and fell back to --gate-file.", "decision": "Renamed the intake id to vagueness-gate and the file to CHANGE-0144-vagueness-gate.md; duplicate doc ids back to 0. ACCOUNTING SPLIT, recorded rather than hidden: the Planning and TDD runs were already appended under ref spec-vagueness-gate before the rename, so this ride's telemetry is split across two ref ids. I did not re-record them under the new ref - that would double-count tokens in METRICS - and I did not hand-edit STATE, which is forbidden. Remaining roles are recorded under vagueness-gate.", "residual": "METRICS will show two partial refs for one ride until a future flush-time reconciliation; the ride's real cost is the sum. A follow-up covers making the collision impossible rather than merely corrected.", "source": "TDD report deviation 1, 2026-08-14T01:14Z; docs-audit duplicate-doc-ids section"}
