{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-14T15:38:32Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-range-mode-dirty-worktree","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"range mode takes added-line numbers from git diff base...HEAD but reads file content from the worktree, so a dirty tree reports an untouched symbol and misses the changed ones","decision":"Validation round 3 F17, reproduced with a dirty-worktree fixture; bounded to range mode with uncommitted edits and inherited from the frozen spec D3/D4 design rather than an implementation infidelity, so it was not a blocker; wants a dirty-worktree range fixture","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260814T144556Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine-round3.md"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-14T16:06:04Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-cliflag-kind-precision","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"extractCliFlags labels every --lowercase-flag token 'cli-flag' regardless of context: on the real tree 30 of 139 cli-flag candidates are CSS custom properties (--accent, --bg, --fg, --muted, --line, --card-bg in generate-docs-hub.mjs / generate-factory-report.mjs) and 35 are flags this repo passes TO external tools (git/gh), not CLI surface of this repo at all -- ~47% of the kind, ~17% of all 390 candidates, carry a factually wrong kind label","decision":"an operator triaging the --all list per the class-4 action ('Remove; file an intake note if genuinely valuable') could delete a CSS custom property believing it is an unrequested CLI flag, silently breaking a page's dark theme; no LIMITS sentence warns that the cli-flag kind includes non-flags. Fix is a design call (rename the kind vs exclude --x: / var(--x) contexts) adjacent to the spec's NO STOPLIST decision, so it is deferred rather than fixed in this remediation pass","source":"docs/ai/reviews/review-20260814T154415Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine.md NB-2"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-14T22:22:40Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-validation-staleness-undetected","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"a validation pass survives a later remediation that rewrites the validated code, and the default routing skips re-validation","decision":"Round 3 passed at 15:37Z; code review then failed and remediation rewrote the engine, suite, prompt and eight surfaces, yet SPEC-0012 G3 routing sends a pass-with-review-reset straight to rule 13 and never re-fires rule 11. Only the validator noticing its own staleness caught it, and clearing it needed an owner-approved reset-block --force. The verdict should carry the content hash it was taken against so staleness is mechanical, not a matter of an agent volunteering it","source":"observed 2026-08-14, owner decision recorded; state.mjs reset-block refusal message"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T07:03:31Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-subagent-long-wait-never-wakes","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"a subagent waiting on a long background process can miss its own completion and stall indefinitely, holding the whole ride","decision":"Twice in one ride: round 3 armed three backstop waiters that all watched for a Total: line the framework prefixes with colour codes, and round 4 slept five hours after its sweep had already written summary.txt with 79/79. The coordinator read the tally off disk in seconds. Long-running work should be polled from the artifact on disk, never awaited through a pattern-matched waiter","source":"observed 2026-08-14/15, tests/skills/results/test-20260814-223516/summary.txt written 23:07:42Z, agent silent until 03:59Z"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T07:03:31Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-subagent-probe-hits-real-repo","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P1","finding":"a validator probe helper ran git commands against the real repository and created two commits on main","decision":"The helper cd-ed into a fixture inside a command substitution, which runs in a subshell, so the parent shell stayed in the real repo. Repaired with git reset --mixed 5116c36 and verified independently (HEAD restored, main equals origin main, tag intact, nothing pushed), but nothing structurally prevented it: a read-only role mutated the shipping repo and only caught it by luck","source":"validation round 4, 2026-08-14; coordinator verification of HEAD 5116c36 and zero unpushed commits"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T08:14:24.000Z","actor":"ales_holubec.net","type":"hitl_decision","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","decision":"Narrow the class-4 extractor kinds to CONTRACT surfaces only. Drop or default-off mjs-export, sh-func and ps1-func; keep cli-flag (with the CSS-custom-property and external-tool-flag misclassification fixed) and yaml-key.","rationale":"Owner call 2026-08-15: an internal helper is ABSENT from every spec by design, so absence carries no signal for it — the premise only holds for surfaces a requirement is expected to name. Measured: mjs-export 128 + sh-func 64 + ps1-func 53 = 245 of 390 candidates come from kinds that are categorically wrong, matching the review-measured 245 internal helpers; yaml-key was the one kind where suppression discriminated.","authority":"owner","amends":"frozen spec D3 extractor-kind set and its dependent AC rows","acceptance":"every remaining candidate must be defensible in one sentence stating why a requirement should have named it; raw count expected to drop from 390 to tens","origin_error":"intake assumption A2 listed five extractor kinds without asking whether each is a contract surface; Planning inherited it and validation checked fidelity to a spec that was wrong"}
