{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-16T14:48:17Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-close-after-merge-bypasses-ci","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"running the close ceremony after the merge instead of on the branch puts the close, autogen and telemetry commits straight onto main with no CI","decision":"SKILL_PR step 5c orders PR then close then CI then merge, but merge is the one step the agent does not own, so a directed merge can jump the queue with nothing checking. On PR 260 three commits landed on main under a required-status-check bypass; the previous ride PR 259 did it correctly, so this is an ordering hazard, not a broken rule. Cheapest guard: close-work-item already receives the PR number, so it can read that PR state and say loudly when it is already merged. Degrade-and-report, never a block","source":"observed 2026-08-16, commits f51a991 ea85d5c e894b4b vs merge c824367"}
