{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T16:38:52Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-armcount-inline-comment","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P3","finding":"TEST-027 arm_table still counts an ok=0 that sits in a TRAILING comment on an otherwise live line","decision":"V-5's tightening skips full-line comments and requires an ok=0 assignment, which kills the '# ok=0' padding attack; a trailing '; # ok=0' on a live line would still inflate the count, and closing it needs shell-quote-aware parsing that is more fragile than the hole is worth","source":"tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh arm_table (V-5 remediation, 2026-08-18); limitation stated in that function's header comment"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T16:38:52Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-bare-main-baseref-sweep","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P2","finding":"No guard stops a NEW test or script from pinning a bare 'main' ref that silently never resolves on a pull_request checkout","decision":"Fourth occurrence of this exact class in this repository (TEST-024, the follow-ups suite, test-aai-spec-lint.sh, now test-aai-deslop.sh TEST-027/028); each time it was found by review or validation, not by a check, and each time the affected guard degraded to PASS or to a false reason on CI","source":"validation round 2 findings V-3/V-4 on spec-deslop-corpus-honesty; docs/knowledge/LEARNED.md 2026-07-19; repo-wide sweep for git show/diff/rev-parse against a literal main is out of this scope"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T18:07:02Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-ride-cost-invisible-in-flight","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P2","finding":"scope_cost in generate-factory-report.mjs aggregates only CLOSED rides, so an in-flight ride's cost cannot be read","decision":"the stop-or-continue decision happens mid-ride; a readout that only appears after close cannot inform it, which is the exact motivation CHANGE-0148 was built on","source":"2026-08-18: deslop-corpus-honesty absent from docs/ai/factory-report-data.json scope_cost while in_progress; cost had to be hand-summed from subagent return records"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T20:52:13Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-suite-additivity-guard","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P3","finding":"No mechanical guard remains that a pre-existing arm or assertion in tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh is not removed: TEST-027 (test_027_suite_stays_green_and_additive) was mechanized four times, failed independent validation four times, and was withdrawn 2026-08-18, taking the suite-additivity clause of Spec-AC-06 with it.","decision":"Six distinct defeats across the four attempts: (1) a self-referential known_tests array grepped against the very file that declared it, mutation-proven inert; (2) a bare main base that does not resolve on a pull_request checkout, whose read failure took a SKIP path and reported PASS; (3) unguarded base-side parsers arm_table and main_dispatch_body, three single-token mutations each leaving the per-arm loop vacuous at full-suite exit 0; (4) an unguarded $self read - all eight round-4 cross-checks constrained the BASE reading and none the $self reading, so the one line self_table=$main_table defeated the arm without touching a parser or a cross-check; (5) an arm moved into an unreachable branch inside main() still read as wired, because the wiring check matches text rather than reachability; (6) an arm whose base assertion-site count is 0 clears the per-arm floor unconditionally. Conclusion: an in-file guard cannot verify its own file, since every layer is a reader defined in the artifact it guards. A real fix needs an out-of-file checker that reads the suite AS DATA from a different artifact - none exists today.","source":"scope deslop-corpus-honesty, validation rounds 1-4 (findings V-1, V-3, V-5..V-9 and round 4); docs/specs/SPEC-DRAFT-spec-deslop-corpus-honesty.md Spec-AC-06 WITHDRAWN entry plus GUARD HISTORY; arm removed from tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh on 2026-08-18 (29 arms to 28, committed base has 21 and never carried the guard)"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T20:52:21Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-close-before-push-ordering","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P2","finding":"The PR ceremony ordering - run close-work-item.mjs BEFORE the push, not after - is currently only a habit; nothing enforces it, so a ride can push first and then spend a round chasing framework reds that the close would have cleared.","decision":"Validation round 4 of this scope proved empirically that the 5 tests/skills/test-framework.sh reds are ride-caused and clear only once close-work-item.mjs has run; when the push lands first those reds are read as genuine CI failures and cost a diagnostic round every ride. Make the ordering a gate in the close ceremony (SKILL_PR step order plus a precondition check) rather than prose an agent has to remember.","source":"scope deslop-corpus-honesty, validation round 4, 2026-08-18; .aai/SKILL_PR.prompt.md close ceremony; .aai/scripts/close-work-item.mjs; tests/skills/test-framework.sh"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T21:54:31Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up_status","id":"fu-ride-cost-invisible-in-flight","status":"dropped","resolved_by":"deslop-corpus-honesty","source":"DUPLICATE of fu-scope-cost-no-live-view (filed 2026-08-17 from ride-cost-readout code review NB-8, same defect). Dropped in favour of the first-filed id to keep provenance. Carrying forward the escalation argument: the older entry is P3, but the limit was measured live on 2026-08-18 (deslop-corpus-honesty absent from scope_cost while in_progress, cost hand-summed from subagent records) and it defeats the stated headline motivation of CHANGE-0148, so triage should treat fu-scope-cost-no-live-view as P2."}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T21:55:11Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up_status","id":"fu-deslop-armcount-inline-comment","status":"dropped","resolved_by":"deslop-corpus-honesty","source":"MOOT: the subject no longer exists. arm_table() was removed from tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh on 2026-08-18 together with test_027, which was withdrawn after four mechanizations and four validation failures (see fu-deslop-suite-additivity-guard). Verified: 0 occurrences of arm_table in the suite. If an additivity guard is ever rebuilt out-of-file, its counting rule must handle a trailing '# ok=0' on a live line; that constraint is recorded on the surviving item."}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T22:31:51Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-test005-no-exit-assert","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P3","finding":"TEST-005 (no-write proof) never asserts the engine's exit code, so an engine that dies before doing anything passes it vacuously","decision":"a no-write proof that a crashed process satisfies is not proving absence of writes, it is proving absence of a run; TEST-006 covers the exit contract today so AC-06's paired evidence holds, but the window is one line wide","source":"validation round 5 of deslop-corpus-honesty, 2026-08-18, observed while constructing mutation bites for the withdrawn TEST-027's replacement evidence"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T22:47:34Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-spec0132-cmp-wording","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P3","finding":"SPEC-0132 says its no-write and corpus arms compare manifests with cmp, but tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh invokes no cmp command - the comparisons are shell string compares","decision":"A frozen spec describing a verification mechanism the suite does not use misleads any reader who audits the arm against its spec; the same wording was already corrected once in the deslop-corpus-honesty spec and left uncorrected here as out of ride scope","source":"docs/specs/SPEC-0132-spec-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine.md lines 519, 604, 614, 619, 620, 709, 756, 833; round-5 code review NB-6 on docs/ai/reviews/review-20260818T224100Z-deslop-corpus-honesty.md"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T23:33:35Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"remediation_decision","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","finding":"the round-5 validation pass and the code-review pass both predate the post-review remediation (R-7..R-10), which changed .aai/scripts/deslop-unrequested.mjs renderJson and two test arms","decision":"force-reset last_validation and re-validate the delta rather than ship on a stale pass; this is the exact defect recorded as fu-validation-staleness-undetected and knowing it forbids exploiting it","source":"code review NB-1/NB-2 remediation, 2026-08-18"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-19T00:24:53Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-ac02-single-citation","ref_id":"spec-deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P3","finding":"TEST-023's real-tree citation loop depends on a single non-docs/specs citation per symbol (CHANGE-0125 twice, CHANGE-0096 once)","decision":"A status flip, archive or move on either document turns the arm red for a reason unrelated to the corpus rule, and the arm's other real-tree assertion will not go red with it because this ride's own spec keeps the three symbols suppressed from docs/specs; remediation added a diagnostic split that names citation drift vs a real corpus-rule regression, but the arm is still coupled to two specific documents","source":"docs/ai/validation round 6 V-3; tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh test_023_change_and_rfc_documents_suppress"}
