{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T05:24:44Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-append-only-merge-needs-prefix-order","ref_id":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe","severity":"P2","finding":"resolving a merge conflict in the append-only ledger by unioning both sides in the wrong order rewrites existing bytes from the base branch's point of view, even though no record is lost","decision":"measured 2026-08-21: base plus branch-appends plus main-append passed a no-lines-missing check but failed the suite's append-only assertion at byte offset 248943, because the correct invariant is that the base branch must remain a byte-exact PREFIX, not merely a subset; the weaker check is the one a human naturally writes","source":"PR 268, CI run 32448871998, aai-follow-ups FAIL 'existing ledger bytes were rewritten'; fixed by reordering to main-then-branch, main verified as an exact prefix"}
