{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T17:18:14Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-drain-pipe-grep-q-ratchet","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P2","finding":"Drain the 390-occurrence pipe-into-grep-q ratchet in tests/skills to zero, file by file","decision":"The ratchet stops the count RISING but every one of the 390 recorded occurrences is still a latent CI red the day its fixture passes 64 KiB. The drop-in replacement (assert_payload_contains) now exists, so draining is mechanical; it was left out of this scope because a 390-site blanket rewrite is a large diff with real risk of changing what an assertion means.","source":"tests/skills/lib/pipe-grep-q-baseline.tsv (390 occurrences across 38 files, measured 2026-08-21)"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T17:18:14Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-pipe-into-head-sigpipe-class","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P3","finding":"The same 64 KiB SIGPIPE class exists for pipes into head, which this scope neither converts nor ratchets","decision":"grep -q is not the only early-exit consumer: head exits after N lines and kills its writer identically under pipefail. Measured in this ride: a fixture doing yes | head -n 4000 under set -euo pipefail died at 141 before reaching the assertion under test. The intake counted 86 such sites. Different consumer, identical mechanism, and no ratchet covers it.","source":"docs/issues/CHANGE-DRAFT-assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload.md census; reproduced in this ride's shim self-test"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T17:18:14Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-framework-appends-tracked-testruns","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P3","finding":"tests/skills/test-framework.sh appends to the TRACKED docs/ai/tests/test-runs.jsonl on every run, dirtying the shipping repo","decision":"The per-suite tripwire cannot see it: the append happens in generate_summary, after the last suite's after-snapshot. So the one write the framework itself makes to a tracked file is the one write the tripwire is structurally blind to, and every local full run leaves the working tree dirty.","source":"tests/skills/test-framework.sh generate_summary (append to $PROJECT_ROOT/docs/ai/tests/test-runs.jsonl); git check-ignore returns 1 for that path"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T17:27:47Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-ceremony-levels-nearest-miss-30kb","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P2","finding":"test-aai-ceremony-levels.sh TEST-019 pipes a 30048 B flattened spec into grep -q three times — the corpus nearest miss, 46 percent of the pipe buffer","decision":"Runtime census of the full framework (13091 recorded grep -q pipe payloads, 81 suites): this is the single largest real payload, and the next largest is 12604 B. It sits below the 32768 B at-risk floor Spec-AC-01 declared BEFORE the measurement, so this scope correctly did not convert it — but it is the one site whose payload grows every time docs specs validation-cost-calibration grows, and it will cross 64 KiB first. Convert it to assert_payload_contains before it reddens CI.","source":"runtime grep -q census 2026-08-21, tests/skills/test-aai-ceremony-levels.sh lines 1147 1149 1151, 30048 B each"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T17:45:40Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-ratchet-not-selected-on-rise","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P2","finding":"select-suites does not run aai-hygiene-pack when an ordinary suite file gains a pipe-grep-q occurrence, so the new ratchet never gates the PR that violates it","decision":"the RISE case is the ratchet's main purpose; measured: select-suites --files-from tests/skills/test-aai-doctor.sh yields SELECTED aai-doctor + 3 CORE and DROPPED 77, hygiene-pack among them. Only a brand-new suite file (unmapped -> FULL_RUN) is caught pre-merge; a rise inside a baselined file is caught at merge-to-main or the nightly, post-merge. Fix: give aai-hygiene-pack a tests/skills/*.sh glob or make it CORE","source":"validation round1 2026-08-21, node .aai/scripts/select-suites.mjs --files-from <one changed suite>"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T17:45:40Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-pgq-scan-evadable-shapes","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P3","finding":"pgq_scan misses several real forms of the unsafe idiom: multiline pipelines, grep -F -q flag order, an env-var prefix before grep, an intermediate pipe stage, and every .sh outside the non-recursive tests/skills/*.sh glob (tests/skills/lib/, tests/self-hosting/)","decision":"measured on a fixture tree: of 8 planted variants only the plain one-line form was counted. tests/skills/lib/ is named by the spec D1 as the house location for shared suite code, so it is the likeliest next home for a copied idiom and it is unscanned. Also a same-file remove-one-add-one edit is net-zero and produces no verdict at all","source":"validation round1 2026-08-21, scratchpad evade.sh + launder.sh against pgq_scan/pgq_compare"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T18:54:42Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-payload-needle-unbounded-in-message","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P3","finding":"assert_payload_contains bounds the payload at 512 bytes but interpolates the NEEDLE unbounded, so a 5000-byte needle yields a 5040-byte message","decision":"the helper exists to bound failure messages and leaves half the message unbounded; test_100 varies only the payload so no arm sees it","source":"code review of PR for assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload, finding NB-1"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T18:54:42Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-pgq-baseline-duplicate-row-masks-rise","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P3","finding":"pgq_lookup returns the first matching baseline row, so a duplicated row lets a genuine rise be reported as a SHRINK note","decision":"reachable through an ordinary .tsv merge conflict resolved by keeping both sides, and the ratchet then reports an improvement where there is a regression","source":"code review finding NB-2, demonstrated 3 to 5 reported as SHRINK 9 5"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T18:54:42Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-pgq-scan-silent-on-grep-error","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P3","finding":"pgq_scan sends grep stderr to /dev/null and treats a per-file error as count 0, so an unreadable file is reported as an improvement","decision":"violates the degrade-with-a-NOTE rule in AGENTS.md and makes the ratchet fail open on exactly the file it could not measure","source":"code review finding NB-3, chmod 000 reproduces it"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T20:50:12Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-fixture-arg-exceeds-linux-argstrlen","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P2","finding":"an oversize test payload passed as a single argv entry fails on Linux with exit 126: MAX_ARG_STRLEN caps ONE argument at 131072 bytes even though ARG_MAX is far larger, and darwin has no such cap","decision":"green locally red on CI with an exit code that names nothing; the same fixture shape is used wherever a suite builds a payload larger than 128 KiB, and the pipe-buffer work makes such fixtures more common not less","source":"PR 272 CI run 32523365858 job 96900265051; test_100(c) got 126, fixed by reading the payload from a file"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T21:13:27Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-sigpipe-code-differs-by-platform","ref_id":"assertions-must-not-die-on-their-own-payload","severity":"P2","finding":"a writer killed by EPIPE exits 141 on macOS but 1 on Linux when the writer is a bash BUILTIN, because bash reports the builtin's write error instead of dying by the signal","decision":"any arm that pins 141 as the signature of the pipe hazard is red on Linux while the hazard reproduces perfectly; and exit 1 is indistinguishable from a needle that was simply absent, so such an arm cannot say which happened without a small-payload control running FIRST","source":"PR 272 CI run 32525580619; test_101 CONTROL A got 1 where darwin gives 141"}
