{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T00:53:40Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-isolation-degrade-not-a-gate","ref_id":"a-run-must-say-whether-isolation-armed","severity":"P3","finding":"Decide whether a degraded-isolation run should FAIL, as part of the tripwire-deletion scope","decision":"Report-only is argued as correct ONLY while the tripwire is armed; deleting the tripwire removes that condition, so the gating question must be answered by that ride and not silently dropped","source":"docs/specs/SPEC-DRAFT-spec-a-run-must-say-whether-isolation-armed.md section 'Why a degraded run does not fail the run'"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T00:53:40Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-isolation-degrade-not-on-pass-line","ref_id":"a-run-must-say-whether-isolation-armed","severity":"P3","finding":"A degraded suite's own PASS line is not labelled, unlike the tripwire's equivalent label","decision":"The tripwire prints its NOT ATTESTED reason on the suite's own PASS line; a degraded suite prints a NOTE above the line instead, so a reader scanning only result lines sees a bare PASS","source":"tests/skills/test-framework.sh run_test result case; compare fu-tripwire-unarmed-pass-line-unlabelled"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T00:53:40Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-run-id-second-resolution-collides","ref_id":"a-run-must-say-whether-isolation-armed","severity":"P3","finding":"RUN_ID has one-second resolution so two framework runs in the same second share one run_id in the run ledger","decision":"The ledger is read back BY run_id; two records under one id make per-run attribution ambiguous, which the new suites_isolated and suites_degraded fields now depend on","source":"tests/skills/test-framework.sh RUN_ID=test-$(date -u +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S); measured in TEST-105/TEST-106 fixtures"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T01:04:32Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-isolation-suite-not-hermetic","ref_id":"a-run-must-say-whether-isolation-armed","severity":"P2","finding":"test-aai-suite-isolation TEST-001, TEST-003 and TEST-005 inherit AAI_TEST_ISOLATION instead of stating it, so they go red when the operator exports 0","decision":"A spurious red on a legitimate operator setting trains people to ignore this suite; the TEST-101..107 arms added by CHANGE a-run-must-say-whether-isolation-armed now state their isolation explicitly and the SPEC-0138 arms should do the same","source":"measured 2026-08-22: AAI_TEST_ISOLATION=0 bash tests/skills/test-aai-suite-isolation.sh reds TEST-001/003/005 while the framework behaves exactly as designed"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T01:58:06Z","actor":"claude-opus-5","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-seeding-completeness-uncounted","ref_id":"a-run-must-say-whether-isolation-armed","severity":"P2","finding":"a partly-seeded disposable checkout is reported isolated in all three surfaces, and two of its three seeding steps fail with no NOTE at all","decision":"the isolated-degraded axis answers where a suite ran, not whether the copy matched the working tree; a suite silently testing HEAD instead of your edits is the greener-run-that-tests-less failure this scope names, and on the seeding axis there is still no counter, no summary line and no ledger field, while iso_create's untracked-copy and per-dev-seed steps swallow errors under cp || true","source":"tests/skills/test-framework.sh iso_create - one log_warn for the diff replay, two 'cp -p ... || true' silent steps; spec section 'The vocabulary, decided once' defers this deliberately"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T01:58:13Z","actor":"claude-opus-5","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-wrapper-no-repo-root-branch-dead","ref_id":"a-run-must-say-whether-isolation-armed","severity":"P3","finding":"the wrapper's 'no repository root could be resolved' degrade branch is unreachable, so its comment claims three reportable reasons where only two can fire","decision":"aai_iso_is_suite_run matches a candidate against \"$AAI_REPO_ROOT\"/tests/*, which with an empty AAI_REPO_ROOT is the pattern /tests/*; no suite inside a real checkout matches it, so the guarded branch is never entered and such an invocation stays silent rather than reporting degraded","source":".aai/scripts/aai-run-tests.sh lines 299-337, read-derived; AAI_REPO_ROOT is computed at line 111 and is never empty for a resolvable script path"}
