{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T06:47:35Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-seed-path-loss-not-a-gate","ref_id":"a-half-seeded-checkout-says-it-is-isolated","severity":"P3","finding":"a seed path that is on ISOLATION_SEED_PATHS and present in the working tree but absent from the checkout is reported, not gated, so a run can still be green while an assertion silently became a passing skip","decision":"SPEC-0138 measured four assertion groups degrading to passing skips without the seed files; this scope reports the loss but deliberately adds no gate, and the gate needs a per-path arrival assertion this scope does not build","source":"docs/specs/SPEC-DRAFT-spec-a-half-seeded-checkout-says-it-is-isolated.md section 'Why an incomplete seed does not fail the run'"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T07:09:10Z","actor":"claude-opus-5","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-seeding-skipped-token-collides","ref_id":"a-half-seeded-checkout-says-it-is-isolated","severity":"P3","finding":"The seeding axis's third token 'skipped' collides with two existing uses of the same word in the SAME summary block","decision":"One block now prints 'Skipped: N (P%)' (a suite that exited 42), 'not attested (skipped, failed, ...)' (the tripwire reusing that meaning) and 'Seeding: ... N skipped' (no checkout was made). Meanings 1 and 2 agree; meaning 3 is unrelated, so a human reader needs a legend where a machine reader does not. The spec's names-considered section rejected six alternatives but never checked the word against the framework's own result counter.","source":"validator probe H: one run printed 'Skipped: 1 (50%)' and 'Seeding: 0/2 suite(s) fully seeded; 2 partial; 0 skipped' in the same block; real 81-suite-shape run also carries the tripwire parenthetical"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T07:09:19Z","actor":"claude-opus-5","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-seed-arms-vanish-when-lever-dead","ref_id":"a-half-seeded-checkout-says-it-is-isolated","severity":"P3","finding":"TEST-110, TEST-111 and TEST-112 abandon the whole arm with no verdict when the chmod-000 lever cannot work","decision":"seed_make_unreadable returns 1 and every caller writes '|| return', so on a host where file mode denies the user nothing (a root container) those three arms print NOT COVERED and then emit neither log_pass nor log_fail. The suite has no arm-count check, so it still prints 'All tests passed!' with three of six new arms silently absent. The convention they cite - TEST-004(d) and TEST-113(b) - uses if/else and keeps the arm's verdict.","source":"read of tests/skills/test-aai-suite-isolation.sh seed_make_unreadable and its three '|| return' callers, against the if/else at TEST-004(d) line 387 and TEST-113(b) line 1419; suite main() has no registered-arm tally"}
