{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T07:15:37Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-seed-loss-turns-an-arm-into-a-skip","ref_id":"a-half-seeded-checkout-says-it-is-isolated","severity":"P2","finding":"a seed path present in the working tree but absent from the checkout leaves the run GREEN at exit 0 while a suite reads an empty file, so an assertion silently becomes a passing skip","decision":"restated at P2 from the dropped P3 on validation's judgement, which reproduced it (probe J: the suite read an empty seed file and the run stayed green); this is coverage loss that reports itself only as a NOTE, and the same under-severity criticism was made of the sibling axis one ride ago","source":"validation round 1 of a-half-seeded-checkout-says-it-is-isolated, 2026-08-22; input to the tripwire-deletion scope"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-22T16:25:56Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-seed-step2-enumeration-silent","ref_id":"spec-a-half-seeded-checkout-says-it-is-isolated","severity":"P3","finding":"Seeding step 2 reports seeded when git ls-files could not enumerate part of the tree (unreadable directory), so files silently never copied are counted as a complete seed","decision":"Both funnels send ls-files stderr to /dev/null and it exits 0 with only a warning, so the run prints the all-clear Seeding line and AAI-SEEDING: seeded while untracked content under that directory never reached the checkout - the same false-completeness claim this axis was built to remove, one level up","source":"code review 2026-08-22: measured on git in a scratch repo - chmod 000 on a directory containing an untracked file gives \"warning: could not open directory sub/: Permission denied\" and rc=0 with the file absent from the listing; tests/skills/test-framework.sh:366 and .aai/scripts/aai-run-tests.sh:410 both discard that stderr"}
