{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-23T16:51:44Z","actor":"validation","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-haz-arm-cardinality-not-uniqueness","ref_id":"the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards","severity":"P3","finding":"test_083's anti-vacuity guard checks array LENGTH (>=5) on HAZ_IDS/HAZ_SCARS, not distinctness or non-triviality, so it is satisfiable while still asserting nothing for one slot","decision":"reproduced in isolation (bash 3.2 and the extracted hazards_findings function): replacing HAZ-WORKTREE with a duplicate HAZ-LEDGER keeps both arrays at length 5, the cardinality guard passes, and hazards_findings never reports MISSING-HAZ-WORKTREE because that anchor is simply never iterated -- the arm is green while HAZ-WORKTREE is uncovered. A second, independent reproduction: replacing every HAZ_IDS entry with a bare space keeps length 5 and the space token trivially matches any non-empty section body, so none of the five HAZ_IDS slots is actually being verified for its real identity. This is the exact failure class (cardinality satisfied, coverage not) that fu-haz-arm-vacuous-on-empty-corpus fixed for the fully-empty case; the fix's own predicate (>=5 count) does not close the duplicate/degenerate-content variant of the same hole. Lower severity than the original blocker because the attack requires deliberately crafted content in a short, visually-inspectable literal array (a duplicate or all-space entry is easy to spot in code review), unlike the empty-array case which passed silent CI review once already.","source":"reproduced 2026-08-23 in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ales-Projects-aai/9a8e6960-b8be-4819-a998-725da0d91525/scratchpad/test_harness.sh against the real .aai/SUBAGENT_CONTRACT.md at 2350324, extracting hazards_section/hazards_findings verbatim from tests/skills/test-aai-hygiene-pack.sh; validation round 2 of the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-23T16:58:54Z","actor":"validation","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-ac-table-flip-trips-false-open","ref_id":"the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards","severity":"P2","finding":"VALIDATION.prompt.md step 8a's EXCEPTION only defers the ac_evidence EVENT emission for an open slug-id (unnumbered DRAFT) spec; it does not warn against populating the AC Status table's Status/Evidence columns to done, but doing so ALONE (with zero events emitted) already trips docs-audit's probable-false-open Arm A ('AC Status table fully terminal with evidence') and broke tests/skills/test-aai-doc-numbering.sh TEST-013's repo-wide CLEAN regression backstop","decision":"reproduced live in this validation round: editing docs/specs/SPEC-DRAFT-spec-the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards.md's five AC rows to done+Evidence (no ac_evidence event appended) flipped node .aai/scripts/docs-audit.mjs --check from CLEAN to NEEDS-TRIAGE (1 item, verdict probable-false-open, evidence string 'AC Status table fully terminal with evidence') and failed TEST-013 ('Expected CLEAN in repo-audit.log'); reverting the table edit alone (no git restore, plain re-edit) restored CLEAN and TEST-013 green. This is the same failure class CHANGE-0028's review NON-BLOCKING-1 (2026-07-17, docs/ai/reviews/review-20260717-091525.md) flagged for the EVENT path; the fix implemented since then (the current step-8a EXCEPTION text) only covers that one path, so the same self-flag is still reachable through the table-edit path step 8a's own instruction invites ('Evidence column populated')","source":"measured 2026-08-23, validation round 2 of the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards: docs-audit --check verdict CLEAN before edit, NEEDS-TRIAGE (probable-false-open) after editing the AC table alone, CLEAN again after reverting; tests/skills/test-aai-doc-numbering.sh TEST-013 FAIL then PASS across the same edit/revert; docs/ai/decisions.jsonl line 38 (CHANGE-0028 review_disposition, ts 2026-07-17T09:19:43Z) for the pri