{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-23T17:10:48Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-learned-baseline-head-not-main","ref_id":"the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards","severity":"P2","finding":"Both rewritten LEARNED entries (lines 37 and 55) name a worktree 'cut from HEAD' as the baseline for deciding whether a failure is pre-existing, but the advice they replaced named main ('stash/main comparison'); line 54-55 asserts 'FAILS on clean main' in the same sentence that names HEAD as the tree it was reproduced in","decision":"On a feature branch with committed work, HEAD is the role's own work, not the clean baseline. A validator follows the entry, sees prompt-diet TEST-010 fail in a HEAD worktree, concludes 'pre-existing, out of scope' and ships a regression it caused. The fix is 'git worktree add --detach <path> main' (or the merge-base), not the default HEAD","source":"docs/knowledge/LEARNED.md:37-38,55; git worktree add --detach defaults to HEAD; review-20260823T171026Z"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-23T17:10:48Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-learned-worktree-rule-overbroad","ref_id":"the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards","severity":"P2","finding":"LEARNED.md:144-146 hardens 'prefer worktree isolation' into 'HAZ-RESTORE prohibits it outright; use a disposable worktree for any git-mutating role' — but HAZ-RESTORE prohibits restoring git commands on tracked files, it says nothing about working inline","decision":"It misattributes a broader rule to HAZ-RESTORE and contradicts live canon in the same payload: this very spec records 'Worktree recommendation: not_needed / User decision: inline', and SKILL_CODE_REVIEW.prompt.md supports worktree.user_decision == inline as a first-class mode. A dispatched role now reads an absolute prohibition and its own dispatch's exemption together — the exact contradiction class this scope exists to remove","source":"docs/knowledge/LEARNED.md:144-146 vs .aai/SUBAGENT_CONTRACT.md:13-17 and SPEC-DRAFT-spec-the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards.md:143-144; review-20260823T171026Z"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-23T17:11:05Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-protocol-states-stale-60-line-cap","ref_id":"the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards","severity":"P3","finding":".aai/SUBAGENT_PROTOCOL.md:6 describes the CONTRACT as 'the ~60-line duty sheet'; the file now ships at 84 lines, so the sibling canon page the CONTRACT header points at states a cap 40 percent below the shipped one","decision":"This is the fourth place stating the cap; the spec's D1 says the re-base lands 'in the three places that assert it', so the sweep that produced that number missed a live canon surface (it is prose, not a comparison, so no suite catches it). The spec scoped SUBAGENT_PROTOCOL.md out before anyone noticed line 6 stated the number","source":"/usr/bin/grep -n '~60-line' .aai/SUBAGENT_PROTOCOL.md; wc -l .aai/SUBAGENT_CONTRACT.md = 84; review-20260823T171026Z"}
