{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-23T17:11:05Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-contract-cap-counts-lines-not-bytes","ref_id":"the-subagent-contract-omits-the-hazards","severity":"P3","finding":"The CONTRACT cap and its headroom guard count LINES while the cost they proxy is bytes/tokens; on breaching 84 the section was brought back under by unwrapping prose rather than by saying less (lines 7 and 11 are 117 and 125 chars against ~78 for every other prose line in the section)","decision":"The '>=6 lines of headroom below the 90 cap' that TEST-020 reports is nominal: the same three lines can be reclaimed again by rewrapping, so the guard can be satisfied indefinitely without reducing payload cost. Nothing was lost in this instance (the 3 saved lines map exactly to 3 unwrapped lines) but the guard does not measure what D1 argues about","source":"awk length over .aai/SUBAGENT_CONTRACT.md at f46502e/cade339/2350324: lines 53->83->84, bytes 2752->4739->4795, maxlen 191 throughout; review-20260823T171026Z"}
