{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-23T20:05:00Z","actor":"ales_holubec.net","type":"hitl_decision","ref_id":"the-tripwire-is-permanent-not-transitional","supersedes":{"ts":"2026-08-19T16:59:51Z","ref_id":"suites-must-not-touch-the-shipping-repo","type":"hitl_decision"},"supersedes_quote":"when that lands, the tripwire, its known-offender ratchet and the ratchet-path hashing are to be DELETED and every follow-up about them closed as moot","finding":"The successor named by the 2026-08-19 decision LANDED (SPEC-0138, one disposable worktree per suite) and does not remove the cause. Re-measured first-hand on main at 07e6d81 in a throwaway worktree: git rev-parse --git-common-dir inside a disposable worktree returns the SHIPPING repository's .git, and its dirname is the shipping working tree. Isolation relocates a suite's cwd and script path; it does not remove the suite's reach, and any absolute path a suite already holds still resolves. A suite that writes through that path dirties the shipping repository while the run correctly reports isolated - degraded cannot fire, because nothing degraded. Filed as fu-isolated-suite-reaches-shipping-repo (P1). The retirement scope that tried to act on the 2026-08-19 decision measured the counterfactual end to end: with the tripwire deleted and the proposed degraded-gate in place, a run exits 0 at Passed: 2 (100%) / 0 degraded WITH THE WRITE LANDED, and it stopped on its own AC-002 rather than proceed.","decision":"SUPERSEDES the 2026-08-19T16:59:51Z hitl_decision. The tripwire, its known-offender ratchet and the ratchet-path hashing are PERMANENT: their removal is not scheduled and no scope may plan for it or defer a defect on the grounds that they are about to go. The 2026-08-19 entry stays exactly as written - it recorded what was believed and approved on that date, on the evidence available then; it is withdrawn by this later entry, not edited. Exactly ONE registry item closes on this decision: fu-tripwire-removal-needs-a-gate (P2), whose whole content was a precondition for a deletion that is no longer planned. FIFTEEN other open tripwire defects are NOT resolved by it - they are defects in a layer that now stays, listed by id in the spec so nobody re-derives the set, and they have lost their standing excuse rather than been fixed.","reopens_when":["1. fu-isolated-suite-reaches-shipping-repo (P1) is closed with evidence that a suite running under isolation CANNOT reach the shipping working tree - measurable form: from inside the suite's checkout, no run-time-computable path resolves into the shipping tree, where today dirname $(git rev-parse --git-common-dir) does in one call.","2. The counterfactual is re-measured WITH THE TRIPWIRE REMOVED: a fixture suite that writes an absolute path into the shipping tree makes the run exit non-zero. Today that same counterfactual exits 0 at Passed: 2 (100%) / 0 degraded with the write landed.","3. The isolation report is a GATE, shipped in the SAME change that deletes the tripwire and never after. This is the entire content of fu-tripwire-removal-needs-a-gate, restated here so closing that item loses nothing."],"reopens_note":"All three must be measured true, in that order. Anything short of all three leaves the tripwire armed. A decision that says never with no condition is a mood, not a decision.","authority":"owner","approval":"Owner approved this reversal in the 2026-08-23 session, on the measurement above rather than on appetite. The approval is recorded NEXT TO the measurement, not instead of it: the approval is what makes reversing a recorded owner decision legitimate, the measurement is what makes it correct.","residual":"docs/ai/decisions.jsonl is append-only and has no back-pointer, so a reader who reaches the 2026-08-19 line alone still sees a withdrawn claim with no marker on it. Mitigated, not fixed, by supersedes_quote above reproducing that entry's removal sentence verbatim - a grep for the old claim's text now returns TWO lines, the later one withdrawing the earlier - and by dated CORRECTION blocks in every document that cited the old decision.","source":"docs/specs/SPEC-DRAFT-spec-the-tripwire-is-permanent-not-transitional.md; docs/issues/CHANGE-DRAFT-the-tripwire-is-permanent-not-transitional.md; worktree --git-common-dir probe re-taken 2026-08-23 on main 07e6d81; fu-isolated-suite-reaches-shipping-repo (P1)"}
